  "id": "adherence",
  "term": "adherence",
  "definition": "Adherence is the extent to which a person consistently keeps up with a prescribed treatment, such as taking medication and following related care routines over time. In this context, it can be affected by everyday self-perceived cognitive difficulties and by the amount of practical and emotional support a person feels they have.",
